{"availability":"available","full":"andreihar/taibun-demo","name":"taibun-demo","description":"Taiwanese Hokkien Transliterator and Tokeniser","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":4,"forks":2,"created":"2024-05-19T06:21:52Z","updated":"2025-12-12T01:30:02Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://taibun.andreihar.com","topics":["mantine","react","taigi","taiwanese","transliterator"],"demo":"https://taibun.andreihar.com/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T06:36:36.012Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T06:36:36.012Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T06:36:36.012Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T01:26:09.789Z","stars":4,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-08T06:36:36.012Z","stars":4,"forks":2}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Taiwanese Hokkien Transliterator and Tokeniser","App to customise transliteration and retrieve any necessary information about Taiwanese Hokkien pronunciation.","Taibun is a comprehensive tool for transliterating and tokenising Taiwanese Hokkien. Developed as a demo for the Taibun library, this web application showcases its capabilities by allowing users to customise the transliteration of Chinese characters and retrieve detailed pronunciation information."],"features":["Transliterator Page allows users to convert Chinese characters to the chosen transliteration system with customisable parameters such as system, dialect, tone format, delimiter, sandhi rules, and punctuation style.","Tokeniser Page performs tokenisation of Taiwanese Hokkien sentences, breaking down the text into individual words or tokens.","Set Converter Page converts text between Simplified and Traditional Chinese characters for Taiwanese Hokkien.","Users can switch between English, Taiwanese, and Mandarin from the language selector in the Navbar."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/andreihar/taibun-demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"900048cd9b2190d5b1d0b5e55f85233510abd6df25127b8a5250c75cf1c4